{"id":"windows/settings/display-language","platform":"windows","kind":"csp","surface":"settings","identifier":"display-language","name":"Display Language","description":"Windows MDM settings in the Display Language category, applied as OMA-URI (SyncML) values.","group":"Microsoft Office 2016","properties":[{"key":"L_AllowNonAdminUserInstallLAPs","name":"Allow users who aren’t admins to install language accessory packs (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting controls whether users can install language accessory packs for Office even if they don’t have local administrator permissions on their devices. By default, users must have local administrator permissions on their devices to install language accessory packs.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting, users will be able to install language accessory packs for Office even if they don’t have local administrator permissions on their devices. They can install those language accessory packs by going to File > Options > Language in the app, such as Word.\n\nIf you disable or don’t configure this policy setting, users who don’t have local administrator permissions on their devices won’t be able to install language accessory packs. Someone with local administrator permissions on the device will need to install the language accessory packs for the user.\n\nFor more information, see https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/p/?linkid=2161939.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v10~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_Languagesettings~L_Displaylanguage/L_AllowNonAdminUserInstallLAPs","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v10"},{"key":"L_ChangeOrDeleteLinkToLanguagePackDownloadSite","name":"Change or delete link to language pack download site (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting affects the language download link under the display and help language section.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting you, you may enter the URL to another location where language packs may be downloaded.\n\nIf you disable this policy setting the URL will be removed.\n\nIf you do not configure this policy setting, the URL will remain available and point to the language pack download site on Office.com.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_Languagesettings~L_Displaylanguage/L_ChangeOrDeleteLinkToLanguagePackDownloadSite","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v2"},{"key":"L_ChangeOrDeleteLinkToProofingToolsDownloadSite","name":"Change or delete link to the proofing tools download site (User)","type":"enum","description":"This policy setting affects the proofing tools link under the Editing language section.\n\nIf you enable this policy setting you, you may enter the URL to another location where proofing tools may be downloaded.\n\nIf you disable this policy setting the URL will be removed.\n\nIf you do not configure this policy setting, the URL will remain available and point to the proofing tools site on Office.com.","defaultValue":0,"enum":[{"value":"0","description":"Disabled"},{"value":"1","description":"Enabled"}],"address":"./User/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/office16v2~Policy~L_MicrosoftOfficeSystem~L_Languagesettings~L_Displaylanguage/L_ChangeOrDeleteLinkToProofingToolsDownloadSite","scope":"user","introducedIn":"CSP 5.0","source":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-office16v2"},{"key":"L_displayhelpin336","name":"Display help in (User)","type":"enum","description":"","defaultValue":"0","enum":[{"value":"0","description":"(same as menus and dialog boxes)"},{"value":"1078","description":"Afrikaan